<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barquq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1399</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as al-Zahir Barquq</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Barquq was a Circassian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> who became sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in 1382, founding the Burji line of sultans. Briefly deposed in 1389, he regained the throne in 1390 and ruled until his death in 1399. He resisted the advance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> in Syria and built a large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasa</a> and khanqah complex in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>, and his reign began more than a century of Circassian rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/barquq.jpg" alt="Barquq" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moh hakem · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barqouqy_mosque_-_Moez_street.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
